Sorry, I should have explained it a little more.

800/20 = 40 means
 a food ration has 800 nutrition
 and weighs 20 weight units
 for a nutrition ratio of 40 n/w

The nutrition ratio measures how "dense" the food is, or how efficient
the food is at providing nutrition.

The listing was sorted by nutrition ratio, because that's the
interesting number if you're trying to decide what to carry in your
pack, and what to eat first.  Carrying 1 food ration is equivalent to
carrying 20 fortune cookies: they weigh the same and have the same
nutritional value.

And 4 lembas wafers have the same weight as 1 food ration, but provide
4 times the nutrition.  Lembas wafers are very good.
